    (9, None, '\'I just need to borrow a little.\' The term for "borrow" comes from the same root as "busy", because the money occupies you. Russians use one word to borrow and another to lend. Barinov says "a little", but he means thousands.'),
    (10, None, '\'Chef, you want my tips?\' Kostya says "you want" the polite way. He can\'t believe it. His voice rises at the end, and what Russian calls "my" sits in front of "tips". It\'s a very Russian reaction: disbelief with no question word.'),
